<title>GERMANY: Hoechst -97 sales to fall due restructuring.</title>
<headline>Hoechst -97 sales to fall due restructuring.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG on Wednesday forecast that its group sales would drop to between 42 and 47 billion marks in 1997 from 50.9 billion marks in 1996 because of divestments of business.</p>
<p>Chairman Juergen Dormann made the forecast at a news conference.</p>
<p>He added that the scale of the decline would depend on the extent of the restructuring measures undertaken.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
